  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "We substitute each value into the given inequality and check to see if the resulting statement is true or false.\n\n- We substitute the value $w=24$ into the given inequality. We get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{w}{4} & <5 \\\\ \\frac{24}{4} & <5 \\\\ 6 & <5\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, substituting $w=24$ into the inequality leads to a **false** statement. \n\nTherefore, $w=24$ **does not satisfy** this inequality.\n\n- We substitute the value $w=20$ into the given inequality. We get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{w}{4} & <5 \\\\ \\frac{20}{4} & <5 \\\\ 5 & <5\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, substituting $w=20$ into the inequality leads to a **false** statement. \n\nTherefore, $w=20$ **does not satisfy** this inequality.\n\n- We substitute the value $w=8$ into the given inequality. We get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{w}{4} & <5 \\\\ \\frac{8}{4} & <5 \\\\ 2 & <5\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, substituting $w=8$ into the inequality leads to a **true** statement. \n\nTherefore, $w=8$ **satisfies** this inequality.",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
